30acff6d-9b40-4b7c-871f-c95a4926734b,2026-08-18T12:11:02.738Z,31256552,3,"U1: I want my study easier for my gud marks
U2: My next exam date is 6 September
U3: Please explain how to solve 2x+y = 10, 3x + 2y = 15","Start by making one variable easy to eliminate. From \(2x+y=10\), solve for \(y\): \[ y=10-2x \] Substitute into \(3x+2y=15\): \[ 3x+2(10-2x)=15 \] \[ 3x+20-4x=15 \] \[ -x+20=15 \] \[ -x=-5 \Rightarrow x=5 \] Now plug \(x=5\) into \(2x+y=10\): \[ 2(5)+y=10 \Rightarrow 10+y=10 \Rightarrow y=0 \] **So",Conceptual,,,,,Academic,,,,1823,62,0.000406,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
