U3: Solve A handwritten algebra problem asks the student to solve the rational equation a/(x − b) + b/(x − a) = 2, with x ≠ a,b.","**Given** \[ \frac{a}{x-b}+\frac{b}{x-a}=2,\qquad x\ne a,b \] Since \(x\ne a,b\), multiply both sides by \((x-a)(x-b)\): \[ a(x-a)+b(x-b)=2(x-a)(x-b) \] Expand: \[ ax-a^2+bx-b^2=2(x^2-(a+b)x+ab) \] \[ (a+b)x-(a^2+b^2)=2x^2-2(a+b)x+2ab \] Bring everything to one side: \[ 2x^2-3(a+b)x+(a+b)^2=0 \] Fac",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1872,64,0.000851,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
