U24: Done the number exceeds twenty five percent of itself by sixty , the number is","Let the number be \(x\). “25% of itself” is \(\frac{1}{4}x\). “The number exceeds 25% of itself by 60” means: \[ x - \frac{1}{4}x = 60 \] Combine like terms: \[ \frac{3}{4}x = 60 \] Multiply both sides by \(\frac{4}{3}\): \[ x = 60 \times \frac{4}{3} = 80 \] **So, the number is \(\mathbf{80}\).**",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,2491,64,0.001099,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
