U4: Solve q.no.7 Question 7 asks to calculate the distance saved by building a direct 26 km highway between cities A and B instead of traveling via city C, using the given perpendicular route lengths AC and CB.","Since \(AC \perp CB\), triangle \(ACB\) is right-angled at \(C\). Given: \[ AC=2x\text{ km},\qquad CB=(2x+7)\text{ km},\qquad AB=26\text{ km} \] Using Pythagoras’ theorem: \[ (2x)^2+(2x+7)^2=26^2 \] \[ 4x^2+4x^2+28x+49=676 \] \[ 8x^2+28x-627=0 \] Solving, \[ x=\frac{-7+\sqrt{1303}}{4}\approx 7.27 \]",Conceptual,,,,,Academic,,,,1921,64,0.000871,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
