U10: 49","**Not 49 — it’s \(\mathbf{39}\).** If the sum is \(400\), then the number of odd numbers added is \(\sqrt{400}=20\). The 20th odd number is: \[ 2\cdot 20 - 1 = 39 \] Check: adding the first 20 odd numbers gives \(20^2=400\). If the last odd number were \(49\), that would be the \(25^\text{th}\) odd ",Conceptual,,,,,Academic,,,,1864,64,0.000848,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
