U5: How can a percentage of a number be taken","**To take a percentage of a number, change the percent to a fraction (or decimal) and multiply.** Example: \(25\%\) of \(80\) - As a fraction: \(25\% = \frac{25}{100}\) \[ \frac{25}{100}\times 80 = 20 \] So **\(25\%\) of \(80\) is \(\mathbf{20}\)**. You can also use decimals: \(25\% = 0.25\), then \",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1797,62,0.000818,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
3e3d2949-b752-42c5-9b08-620ebce24169,2026-08-18T16:29:54.655Z,31151468,4,"U1: Explain me solution A handwritten attempt to factor the quadratic expression 3x² − 4x − 7 by finding factors and grouping terms.
U2: is there is another way
U3: Please please continue
U4: is there is another way is this any formula method","**Yes—there is a direct formula method: the quadratic formula.** For \(3x^2-4x-7=0\), \(a=3,\; b=-4,\; c=-7\). \[ x=\frac{-b\pm\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a} \] Substitute: \[ x=\frac{4\pm\sqrt{(-4)^2-4(3)(-7)}}{6} =\frac{4\pm\sqrt{16+84}}{6} =\frac{4\pm\sqrt{100}}{6} =\frac{4\pm 10}{6} \] So the two solutions",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1838,62,0.000834,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
