U5: State the raoult law","**Raoult’s law:** In an ideal solution, the partial vapour pressure of each component equals its mole fraction in the liquid times the vapour pressure of the pure component: \[ p_i = x_i\,p_i^{\,0} \] So the total vapour pressure is \[ P_{\text{total}}=\sum_i p_i=\sum_i x_i\,p_i^{\,0}. \]",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1803,64,0.000824,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
