U3: to find the tension acting on the string","**For the two-mass (Atwood machine) setup, the tension in the string is** \[ \mathbf{T=\frac{2m_1m_2g}{m_1+m_2}} \] Using Newton’s 2nd law: \[ m_1g-T=m_1a,\qquad T-m_2g=m_2a \] and \[ a=\frac{(m_1-m_2)g}{m_1+m_2} \] Substitute into \(T=m_2g+m_2a\): \[ T=m_2g+m_2\left(\frac{(m_1-m_2)g}{m_1+m_2}\right",Conceptual,,,,,Academic,,,,1875,64,0.000852,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
