U4: Solve questions 13 The image shows question 13, which asks whether a piecewise-defined function is continuous, with the function defined differently for x ≤ 1 and x > 1.","For \[ f(x)= \begin{cases} x+5, & x\le 1,\\ x-5, & x>1, \end{cases} \] the only possible point of discontinuity is \(x=1\), where the rule changes. At \(x=1\): \[ f(1)=1+5=6 \] Left-hand limit: \[ \lim_{x\to1^-}f(x)=\lim_{x\to1^-}(x+5)=6 \] Right-hand limit: \[ \lim_{x\to1^+}f(x)=\lim_{x\to1^+}(x-5)",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1954,64,0.000884,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
