U3: What patterns exist in triangular numbers","**Triangular numbers have several clear patterns:** - **You make each one by adding the next counting number:** \(1,\ 1+2,\ 1+2+3,\dots\) so the gaps are \(+2,\ +3,\ +4,\ +5,\dots\) - **Each triangular number is the sum \(1+2+\cdots+n\):** The \(n\)-th triangular number is \[ T_n=\frac{n(n+1)}{2}. \",Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1766,62,0.000806,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
