759dbf3c-53ed-45e1-99dc-601864b7dd59,2026-08-18T14:46:04.329Z,1,5,"U1: Simply it Tommorow is my exam and I don't know how to do this kinda of ques A handwritten algebra expression involving multiplication of binomials and subtraction: (-2x + 4y)(3x - 2) - (2x + 7y)(x - 4). The student asks for a simple explanation because an exam is tomorrow.
U2: no first bracket is not minus 2
U3: first bracket is 2x + 4y
U4: first bracket is 2x + 4y and the last bracket is X - 4y
U5: first bracket is 2x + 4y and the last bracket is X - Y",\[ (2x+4y)(3x-2)\;-\;(2x+7y)(x-y) \] Expand the first product: \[ (2x)(3x) + (2x)(-2) + (4y)(3x) + (4y)(-2) = 6x^2 - 4x + 12xy - 8y \] Expand the second product: \[ (2x)(x) + (2x)(-y) + (7y)(x) + (7y)(-y) = 2x^2 - 2xy + 7xy - 7y^2 \] \[ = 2x^2 + 5xy - 7y^2 \] Now subtract the whole second product: \,Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1946,64,0.000881,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
