U16: Please explain how to solve 2x+y = 10, 3x + 2y = 15","Set up elimination. From \(2x+y=10\), multiply by 2: \[ 4x+2y=20 \] Now subtract the second equation \(3x+2y=15\) from this: \[ (4x+2y)-(3x+2y)=20-15 \Rightarrow x=5 \] Plug \(x=5\) into \(2x+y=10\): \[ 2(5)+y=10 \Rightarrow 10+y=10 \Rightarrow y=0 \] **Solution:** \(\mathbf{x=5,\ y=0}\).",Lesson_request,,,,,Academic,,,,2037,64,0.000917,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
