U3: What is the integrating factor (I.F.) Solve the ODE, dy/dx + P(y) = Q, where P and Q are functions of x only, by the method of I.F.","**Integrating factor (I.F.)** for a first‑order linear ODE is a function you multiply the whole equation by so that the left side becomes the derivative of a product. For the linear ODE \[ \frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)\,y=Q(x), \] the integrating factor is \[ \text{I.F.}=e^{\int P(x)\,dx}. \] Multiply the ODE ",Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1773,62,0.000808,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
