U4: Please explain how to solve 7x+2=-19","Start with the equation: \[ 7x + 2 = -19 \] 1) **Get rid of the \(+2\)** by subtracting \(2\) from both sides: \[ 7x + 2 - 2 = -19 - 2 \] \[ 7x = -21 \] 2) **Get \(x\) alone** by dividing both sides by \(7\): \[ \frac{7x}{7} = \frac{-21}{7} \] \[ x = -3 \] Quick check: if \(x=-3\), then \(7(-3)+2=-2",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1818,64,0.000830,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
