U7: 6. In the shown figure, what should be the value of mass \( m \) such that 50 kg block remains in static equilibrium? (1) 15 kg (2) 30 kg (3) 50 kg (4) 45 kg A physics multiple-choice question asks for the mass m required to keep a 50 kg block in static equilibrium on a smooth 37° incline, connected","You identified the correct option, ␀\(30\text{ kg}\)␀. Nice! Because the incline is smooth, the 50 kg block needs a tension equal to its component of weight down the slope: \(T=50g\sin37^\circ=50g\times\frac{3}{5}=30g\). For the hanging mass to remain at rest, its tension is \(T=mg\), so \(mg=30g\) ",Conceptual,,,,,Academic,,,,1993,64,0.000900,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
