U5: What is the importance of matrix order in the properties of matrix addition","**Matrix order (size) is important because you can add matrices only when they have the same order.** If \(A\) is of order \(m \times n\) and \(B\) is of order \(p \times q\), then \(A + B\) is defined **only if** \[ m=p \quad \text{and} \quad n=q \] That’s because matrix addition is done **entry-by",Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1765,62,0.000805,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
