U4: Show that expression 4m-1 always gives odd numbers","**To show \(4m-1\) is always odd (for any integer \(m\)):** \(4m\) is always even because it’s a multiple of 4: \[ 4m = 2(2m) \] Now subtract 1: \[ 4m-1 = 2(2m)-1 \] Any number of the form \(2k-1\) (or \(2k+1\)) is **odd**, because it is **1 away from an even number**. So \(4m-1\) is **always odd** ",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1832,62,0.000832,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
