U4: How does scalar multiplication affect the sum of matrices","**Scalar multiplication “distributes” over matrix addition.** If \(A\) and \(B\) are the same size matrices and \(c\) is a scalar, then \[ c(A+B)=cA+cB. \] It also works the other way around: \[ (c+d)A=cA+dA. \] So multiplying a *sum* of matrices by a scalar gives the same result as multiplying each",Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1781,62,0.000812,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
