U6: Explain me more","**\(2x(5+3)\) means “\(2x\) multiplied by the total of \(5\) and \(3\).”** 1) Do the brackets first: \[ 5+3=8 \] 2) Now multiply: \[ 2x \times 8 = 16x \] So the simplified answer is **\(16x\)**. If you want, I can also show the *distributive method* (spreading \(2x\) to both 5 and 3).",Conceptual,,,,,Academic,,,,1796,62,0.000818,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
