12599468-a41b-4aad-8ad1-13c24a357ec4,2026-08-18T11:10:17.864Z,1,3,"U1: According to Arithmetic progression, Find the sum of the first 40 positive integers divisible by 6
U2: According to Arithmetic progression chapters, Find the sum of the first 15multiples of 8
U3: According to Arithmetic progression, Find the first and the last terms of an AP are 17 and 350 respectively.If the common difference is9, how many terms are there and what is their sum","Use the \(n\)th-term idea for an AP: \[ l = a + (n-1)d \] Here \(a=17\), \(l=350\), \(d=9\). So \[ 350 = 17 + (n-1)9 \] \[ 333 = 9(n-1) \] \[ n-1 = 37 \;\Rightarrow\; n = \mathbf{38} \] Now the sum of \(n\) terms: \[ S_n=\frac{n}{2}(a+l)=\frac{38}{2}(17+350)=19\cdot 367= \mathbf{6973} \] **So there ",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1866,64,0.000849,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
