U4: How we will say you want it in malayalam","You can say **“You want it”** in Malayalam in a few common ways, depending on how polite you want to be. ### To a friend (casual, singular) - **നിനക്കത് വേണം.** *ninakk ath vēṇam* Meaning: *You want it.* ### To an elder/teacher (respectful) - **താങ്കൾക്ക് അത് വേണം.** *tāṅkaḷkk ath vēṇam* Meaning: *Y",Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1772,64,0.000811,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Language Learning / Translation,gate_llm,gate_llm
