U7: How to do","Use the kinematics formula (retardation = constant): \[ v^2=u^2+2as \] Train stops, so \(v=0\): \[ 0=u^2+2as \;\Rightarrow\; s=\frac{-u^2}{2a} \] Since \(a\) (retardation) is the same each time, \(s\propto u^2\). If speed is doubled: \(u' = 2u\) \[ s' \propto (2u)^2 = 4u^2 \Rightarrow s' = 4s \] Giv",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,2015,64,0.000908,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
