U3: Please explain how to solve 2x+y = 10, 3x + 2y = 15","Set up the two equations: \[ 2x+y=10 \quad (1) \] \[ 3x+2y=15 \quad (2) \] From (1), get \(y\) alone: \[ y = 10-2x \] Put this into (2): \[ 3x + 2(10-2x) = 15 \] \[ 3x + 20 - 4x = 15 \] \[ -x + 20 = 15 \] \[ -x = -5 \] \[ x = 5 \] Now find \(y\) using \(y = 10-2x\): \[ y = 10 - 2(5) = 10 - 10 = 0 \]",Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1838,64,0.000415,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
