U3: Please explain how to solve 2x+y = 10, 3x + 2y = 15gut","Set up the system: \[ 2x+y=10 \quad (1) \] \[ 3x+2y=15 \quad (2) \] From (1), solve for \(y\): \[ y=10-2x \] Substitute into (2): \[ 3x+2(10-2x)=15 \] \[ 3x+20-4x=15 \] \[ -x+20=15 \] \[ -x=-5 \Rightarrow x=5 \] Now find \(y\) using \(y=10-2x\): \[ y=10-2(5)=0 \] **Answer: \(\mathbf{x=5,\ y=0}\)**",Conceptual,,,,,Academic,,,,1863,64,0.000848,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
