U2: Mister kumar
U3: Please explain how to solve 2x+y = 10, 3x + 2y = 15",Start with the first equation and make \(y\) alone: \[ 2x+y=10 \;\Rightarrow\; y=10-2x \] Now put \(y=10-2x\) into the second equation: \[ 3x+2y=15 \] \[ 3x+2(10-2x)=15 \] Simplify: \[ 3x+20-4x=15 \] \[ -x+20=15 \] \[ -x=-5 \] \[ x=5 \] Plug \(x=5\) back into \(y=10-2x\): \[ y=10-2(5)=10-10=0 \] So ,Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1822,62,0.000828,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
