U3: Prove that root 5 is irrational","**Assume \(\sqrt{5}\) is rational.** Then it can be written in simplest form as \[ \sqrt{5}=\frac{a}{b} \] where \(a\) and \(b\) are integers, \(b\neq 0\), and \(\gcd(a,b)=1\). Square both sides: \[ 5=\frac{a^{2}}{b^{2}} \] Multiply by \(b^{2}\): \[ 5b^{2}=a^{2} \] So \(a^{2}\) is divisible by \(5\)",Unit Conversion,,,,,Academic,,,,1784,64,0.000816,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
