## Internship Report Plan (40–45 pages) 
**Theme:** Survey + Volunteering in Health Camp + Awareness Workshops (Health, Crop Insurance, Life Insurance) 
**Program:** B.Sc. Zoology (3rd Year) — connect it to **public health, community awareness, and field-based learning**.

---

# Front Section (Pages i–vi) *(Roman numbers)*

## **Page i — Cover Page**
**Title:** *Internship Report* 
**Subtitle:** *Health Camp Survey, Volunteering & Awareness Workshops (Health, Crop & Life Insurance)* 
- Your Name 
- B.Sc. Zoology (3rd Year), Dept. of Zoology 
- College: St. Xavier’s College, Ranchi 
- Internship Organization/Host (Name + Place) 
- Duration (From–To) 
- Submitted to (Guide/Teacher name)

## **Page ii — Certificate (College/Organization)**
Paste/attach internship completion certificate (if you have it).

## **Page iii — Declaration (if required)**
1 short paragraph: report is original work, submitted for evaluation.

## **Page iv — Acknowledgement**
Thank: guide, organizer/medical team, survey respondents, workshop resource persons.

## **Page v — Abstract / Executive Summary (½ to 1 page)**
Include:
- What you did (survey + volunteering + workshops)
- Where and when
- Key learning: communication, public interaction, teamwork
- 3–5 key outcomes (ex: number of people surveyed, helped, awareness topics covered)

## **Page vi — Table of Contents**
List all headings with page numbers.

---

# Main Report (Pages 1–40 approx.)

## **Page 1 — Introduction**
Include:
- Meaning of internship for Zoology student (field learning, human health link)
- Why health camps matter (community health, awareness, prevention)
- Your purpose: survey + volunteering + awareness sessions

**Highlight box (1 small box):**
- “Key Focus Areas: Community Survey • Health Camp Support • Awareness Workshops”

---

## **Pages 2–3 — Objectives**
### **2.1 General Objectives**
- Understand community health needs through survey
- Support health camp activities
- Learn awareness communication skills

### **2.2 Specific Objectives (write 8–10 points)**
Examples:
- Collect basic health-related information (age, common issues, awareness level)
- Observe health camp workflow (registration → check-up → advice)
- Assist in crowd management and guidance
- Learn how workshops explain insurance and health schemes
- Improve trust-building and communication in public settings

---

## **Pages 4–5 — Profile of Internship Site/Organizers**
### 3.1 About the Organization/Health Camp Setup
- Location, organizing body
- Type of camp (general health camp, awareness camp, etc.)
- Team involved (doctors, volunteers, staff)

### 3.2 Beneficiaries/Target Group
- Who attended (students, local community, rural/urban, etc.)

**Photo placement**
- **Photo 1 (Page 5):** Banner/entry gate of camp/workshop 
Caption format: *Figure 1: Health camp venue banner (Date, Place).*

---

## **Pages 6–9 — Internship Methodology (Very Important)**
### 4.1 Survey Method
- Survey type: questionnaire/interview (tick what you used)
- Sample size: number of respondents
- Area covered
- Timing: dates and time slots

### 4.2 Tools Used
- Printed form / Google form / notebook
- Consent method (verbal consent)
- Language used (Hindi/English)

### 4.3 Ethical Considerations
- Respect, privacy, no forcing answers
- No sharing personal details

### 4.4 Data Handling
- How you arranged data (tables, charts)
- Simple analysis method (percentages)

**Photo placement**
- **Photo 2 (Page 9):** You doing survey/interacting (avoid showing close-up faces if possible)

---

## **Pages 10–19 — Survey Work (Main Body)**
### 5.1 Survey Theme & Questions (summary)
Write categories (not necessarily all questions):
- Basic demographic info (age group, gender—if taken)
- Health awareness (hygiene, nutrition, check-ups)
- Common health complaints (if collected)
- Awareness of insurance (basic awareness level)

### 5.2 Respondent Profile (Table)
Example headings:
- Age group distribution
- Occupation/student/local resident (if relevant)

### 5.3 Key Findings (Use 4–6 subsections)
Examples:
- 5.3.1 Common health concerns observed/reported 
- 5.3.2 Awareness about preventive health practices 
- 5.3.3 Barriers to healthcare access (time, cost, distance, lack of info) 
- 5.3.4 Awareness of crop/life insurance (low/moderate/high)

### 5.4 Charts/Tables (at least 4–6)
You can add:
- Pie chart: awareness level
- Bar graph: common issues
- Table: yes/no responses

### 5.5 Discussion (Link to Zoology)
Connect survey to:
- health education, disease prevention, nutrition
- importance of awareness for community well-being

**Photo placement**
- **Photo 3 (Page 14):** Group of survey students/team
- **Photo 4 (Page 18):** Survey form sample (blur any personal data)

---

## **Pages 20–27 — Volunteering in Health Camp**
### 6.1 Role and Responsibilities
Write bullet points:
- Registration help
- Guiding patients
- Managing queues
- Helping with basic information desk
- Supporting awareness desk (if any)

### 6.2 Work Flow of a Health Camp (Write as steps)
1. Entry/registration 
2. Basic details recording 
3. Primary check-up (BP, weight etc. if observed) 
4. Doctor consultation 
5. Advice/medicine distribution (if present) 
6. Exit + awareness message

### 6.3 Skills Developed
- Communication and listening
- Teamwork
- Time management
- Empathy and public dealing

### 6.4 Observations (Zoology link)
- Nutrition advice, hygiene, common infections, lifestyle diseases (only generally)
- Importance of awareness and early check-ups

**Photo placement**
- **Photo 5 (Page 22):** Registration/help desk
- **Photo 6 (Page 25):** Crowd management/volunteer badge/team photo

