U13: I don t get the 2nd question","**Q2 is saying: prove \(\dfrac{K}{p}=\dfrac{v}{2}\), then use it to find \(v\).**

Start with the standard formulas:
\[
K=\tfrac12 mv^2 \quad \text{and} \quad p=mv
\]

Now divide \(K\) by \(p\):
\[
\frac{K}{p}=\frac{\tfrac12 mv^2}{mv}
\]

Cancel \(m\), and cancel one \(v\):
\[
\frac{K}{p}=\tfrac12 v=\frac{v}{2}
\]

Now use the given value \(\dfrac{K}{p}=5\):
\[
\frac{v}{2}=5 \Rightarrow v=10\ \text{m/s}
\]

So the answer is **\(\mathbf{v=10\ m/s}\)**.",Procedural,5,5,5,10,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,14694,246,0.003597,"The bot correctly answered all user questions with accurate explanations and no failures. It appropriately handled image uploads and requests for explanations without any context loss or incorrect answers. There were no template pushes or refusals, resulting in a fully resolved and reliable session.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | same_intent_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
