U10: I need answer","**I can’t give the final numerical currents/voltages yet because the right-hand voltage source value is not visible in your photo.** It looks like a source with \(-\) at the top and \(+\) at the bottom, but the **number of volts isn’t readable**, and the answer depends on that value.

If you tell me the right source value (for example “5 V” or “10 V”), I’ll plug it in and give the full numeric results.

Meanwhile, here is the complete solution **in terms of the right source voltage \(V_s\)** (with bottom wire as 0 V):

- Left source is \(+10\text{ V}\) at the top node.
- Right source has \(-\) at top and \(+\) at bottom, so the **top-right node voltage** is \(\;V_R=-V_s\).

Let the middle top node voltage be \(V\). Then the resistor voltages (with your marked polarities) are:
\[
v_1 = 10 - V,\qquad v_2 = V,\qquad v_3 = V - (-V_s)=V+V_s
\]

Currents in the marked directions:
\[
i_1=\frac{v_1}{2}=\frac{10-V}{2}
\]
\[
i_2=\frac{v_2}{8}=\frac{V}{8}
\]
\[
i_3=\frac{v_3}{4}=\frac{V+V_s}{4}
\]

KCL at the middle node (current in from left equals currents out to right and down):
\[
i_1=i_2+i_3
\]
\[
\frac{10-V}{2}=\frac{V}{8}+\frac{V+V_s}{4}
\]

Multiply by 8:
\[
4(10-V)=V+2(V+V_s)
\]
\[
40-4V=3V+2V_s
\]
\[
7V=40-2V_s
\]
\[
\boxed{V=\frac{40-2V_s}{7}}
\]

So the final expressions are:
\[
\boxed{v_2=V=\frac{40-2V_s}{7}\text{ V}}
\]
\[
\boxed{v_1=10-V=10-\frac{40-2V_s}{7}=\frac{30+2V_s}{7}\text{ V}}
\]
\[
\boxed{v_3=V+V_s=\frac{40-2V_s}{7}+V_s=\frac{40+5V_s}{7}\text{ V}}
\]

\[
\boxed{i_1=\frac{10-V}{2}=\frac{30+2V_s}{14}=\frac{15+V_s}{7}\text{ A}}
\]
\[
\boxed{i_2=\frac{V}{8}=\frac{40-2V_s}{56}=\frac{20-V_s}{28}\text{ A}}
\]
\[
\boxed{i_3=\frac{V+V_s}{4}=\frac{40+5V_s}{28}\text{ A}}
\]

