According to traditional stories, Alauddin heard about the beauty of Rani Padmini, the wife of Raja Ratan Singh of Mewar. He became interested in her and sent a message to Ratan Singh asking him to let Alauddin look at her reflection in a mirror. Ratan Singh agreed, and Alauddin saw Rani Padmini’s reflection.

After that, Alauddin attacked the fort, captured Ratan Singh, and demanded Rani Padmini in exchange for his release.

When the people of Mewar heard this, Rani Padmini made a plan. With the help of two brave and trusted men, Gora and Badal, and a group of soldiers dressed as women, Padmini went to rescue the king. Gora and Badal secretly released Ratan Singh and brought him back to the fort.

Alauddin’s large army was stopped by Gora, Badal, and their brave soldiers. The Rajput soldiers fought fearlessly, even when hundreds of them died. They fought for their king, queen, and land.

