**First, I’ll do 2(i) and 2(ii).**

**2(i)** \(2\,\text{m} : 200\,\text{cm} :: 5\,\text{m} : \square\,\text{cm}\)

Since \(1\,\text{m} = 100\,\text{cm}\), \(2\,\text{m} = 200\,\text{cm}\). 
So the left ratio is \(2\,\text{m} : 200\,\text{cm} = 200\,\text{cm} : 200\,\text{cm} = 1:1\).

So \(5\,\text{m}\) must equal \(\square\,\text{cm}\). 
\[
5\,\text{m} = 5\times 100 = 500\,\text{cm}
\]
**Answer: \(\square = \mathbf{500\,\text{cm}}\)**

---

**2(ii)** \(3\,\text{kg} : 3000\,\text{g} :: 7\,\text{kg} : \square\,\text{g}\)

Since \(1\,\text{kg} = 1000\,\text{g}\), \(3\,\text{kg} = 3000\,\text{g}\). 
Again it’s a \(1:1\) match, so \(7\,\text{kg} = \square\,\text{g}\).
\[
7\,\text{kg} = 7\times 1000 = 7000\,\text{g}
\]
**Answer: \(\square = \mathbf{7000\,\text{g}}\)**

