f13e6ee9-e45e-4f83-9254-74652a37ac7a,2026-08-18T16:16:49.601Z,1,5,"U1: find the coordinates of point C which lies on the line ab reduced such that AC equals to BC where the coordinates of point A and B are (- 1,7) and (4,- 3)
U2: find the coordinates of point C which lies on the line ab reduced such that AC=2BC where the coordinates of point A and B are (- 1,7) and (4,- 3)
U3: find the coordinates of point C which lies on the line ab produced such that AC=2BC where the coordinates of point A and B are (- 1,7) and (4,- 3)
U4: Why is solution showing in red
U5: Solve again","**\(\mathbf{C=(9,\,-13)}\)**

“On the line \(AB\) produced” means \(C\) is outside the segment \(AB\). Since \(AC=2BC\), \(C\) must be beyond \(B\) (so \(AC\) is longer than \(BC\)).

Use the external section formula. If \(C\) divides \(AB\) externally in the ratio \(AC:CB = 2:1\), then
\[
C\left(\frac{2x_B-1x_A}{2-1},\ \frac{2y_B-1y_A}{2-1}\right)
\]
With \(A(-1,7)\), \(B(4,-3)\):
\[
x_C=\frac{2(4)-(-1)}{1}=8+1=9
\]
\[
y_C=\frac{2(-3)-7}{1}=-6-7=-13
\]
So \(\mathbf{C=(9,-13)}\).

(Quick check: \(AB=\sqrt{5^2+(-10)^2}=5\sqrt5\), \(BC=\sqrt{5^2+(-10)^2}=5\sqrt5\), \(AC=\sqrt{10^2+(-20)^2}=10\sqrt5=2\,BC\).)",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Speech to Text,,,0.9500,13448,254,0.003330,"The bot correctly answered all user queries with accurate and complete explanations, including handling the difference between internal and external division. There are no detected failures or issues in context handling or answer correctness. The user re-asked for the solution to be repeated, indicating neutral sentiment without explicit frustration.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | same_intent_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
