## Summary (English)
A poor mother who was disliked by the villagers dies suddenly, leaving her three children alone. Neighbours feel pity after her death and arrange the burial. They take the older two children, John and Kate, because they can work and be “useful,” but no one wants to take Maggie, who is sick and bedridden. People suggest sending Maggie to the poorhouse, but it feels cruel for a helpless child. When everyone leaves, Maggie panics at being alone. Joe Thompson, a wheelwright who looks rough but is kind inside, cannot ignore her fear. He goes back, comforts her, and gently carries her to his home. Joe worries because his wife is childless and not very patient or self-sacrificing, so he expects she may not welcome the sick child.

