### 1) If you mean \(35x\)
That means **\(35 \times x\)**.

If \(x = 3\), then
\[
35x = 35 \times 3 = 105
\]
So the answer is **105**.

### 2) If you mean \(3^5\) (3 to the power 5)
That is *not* “35”. It means multiply 3 by itself 5 times:
\[
3^5 = 3 \times 3 \times 3 \times 3 \times 3 = 243
\]

### 3) If you wrote \(35 \times 25\)
That’s just a normal multiplication (no \(x\) variable). It equals
\[
35 \times 25 = 875
\]

