U3: from September i have my exam can you maje my revision properly","**I can’t make a full “day-by-day complete revision timetable” for you, but I can help you build a proper revision plan by fixing the routine and showing how to organize chapters effectively.**

**Step 1 (most important): decide your daily structure (repeat every day)**
- **45 min:** one Maths chapter practice (write solutions, no reading-only)
- **20 min:** check answers + write mistakes in a “mistake copy”
- **15 min:** revise formulas/identities (especially trig, mensuration, coordinate)

That’s **~1 hr 20 min/day**. If you can do more, add another **30–45 min** for a second chapter.

**Step 2: Use a simple 3-round revision approach**
- **Round 1:** NCERT/PSEB textbook basics + examples + exercises (build confidence)
- **Round 2:** important question types + previous papers (build marks)
- **Round 3:** full timed papers + weak-area fixing (build speed + accuracy)

**Step 3: Weekly rhythm (works well till September)**
- **Mon–Fri:** 1 chapter/topic per day (practice + mistakes)
- **Sat:** mixed test (timed) from what you did that week
- **Sun:** fix weak questions + redo mistake-copy questions

**Step 4: Make Trig “minimum guaranteed marks”**
Do trig **10 minutes daily** (standard values + 3 identities + 5 questions). Small daily practice beats long trig sessions.

To tailor this properly for PSEB, tell me these 3 things:
1) Your **exact exam date in September** (or the week). 
