**C)** Numericals ( \(F=ma\), momentum, impulse; Class 9 level)

If you want a quick start right now, here’s the tight core of the chapter:

**Force** is a push or pull that can change an object’s **speed**, **direction**, or **shape**. **Balanced forces** cancel (net force \(=0\)) so motion doesn’t change; **unbalanced forces** give a nonzero net force, so motion changes (acceleration).

**Newton’s Laws:** 
1) **First law (inertia):** If net force is zero, an object stays at rest or keeps moving with constant velocity. 
2) **Second law:** Net force is proportional to rate of change of momentum; for constant mass, \(F=ma\). 
3) **Third law:** Every action has an equal and opposite reaction (on different bodies).

