U9: All composite number","**A composite number is any whole number greater than \(1\) that has more than two factors (it’s not prime).** 

**So “all composite numbers” are:** 
\[
4,\,6,\,8,\,9,\,10,\,12,\,14,\,15,\,16,\,18,\,20,\,21,\,22,\,24,\,25,\,26,\,27,\,28,\,30,\,\dots
\]
(There are infinitely many composite numbers.)

**Quick check:** if a number is divisible by \(2,3,5,7,\dots\) (and it’s bigger than that divisor), then it’s composite.",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,13029,254,0.003258,The bot correctly answered all user questions without any failures or misunderstandings. The session involved academic content with an image upload but no errors or issues were detected. User sentiment is neutral with no explicit feedback indicating frustration or satisfaction.,0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,same_intent_reask | near_duplicate_reask | multiple_similar_requests | gate_llm,gate_llm
