U4: Can area be negative for rectangles","**No—area of a rectangle cannot be negative.** 

Area counts “how much surface” the rectangle covers, so it’s always \( \ge 0 \).

- If the length and width are positive, \(A = l \times w\) is **positive**.
- If one side is \(0\), the “rectangle” is flat, so \(A = 0\).
- If you ever get a negative number, it usually means a sign mistake (for example, using a negative value for a length).",Unit Conversion,5,5,5,10,Academic,,,1.0000,12385,236,0.003071,The bot correctly and clearly answered all user questions without any failures or misunderstandings. There were no indications of user frustration or repeated re-asks due to unsatisfactory answers. The session is a straightforward academic Q&A with no technical or content issues.,0,full_rate,Academic,Concept Explanation,same_intent_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
