Let \(OM\perp AB\) and \(ON\perp CD\).

In right triangles \(\triangle OPM\) and \(\triangle OPN\): 
\(\angle OMP=\angle ONP=90^\circ\) and \(\angle MPO=\angle APO=\angle OPD=\angle OPN\). 
So \(\triangle OPM \sim \triangle OPN\).

Hence \(\dfrac{OM}{ON}=\dfrac{OP}{OP}=1 \Rightarrow OM=ON\).

Chords equidistant from the centre are equal \(\Rightarrow \boxed{AB=CD}\).**",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Speech to Text,,,0.9500,13262,243,0.003275,The bot correctly answered the geometry questions with accurate explanations and no detected failures. The user rephrased the second question but did not indicate dissatisfaction or correction ignored. The session is academic with speech-to-text modality and no bot failures.,0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,multiple_similar_requests | gate_llm,gate_llm
