1fdca8eb-2d03-4a59-b4f1-eb66ffee2803,2026-08-18T15:05:07.667Z,1,3,"U1: Find the area of the quadrilateral whose vertices are at (-9,0) , (-8,6),(-1,-2),(-6,-3) using the formula 1/2(x1y2+x2y3+x3y4+x4y1) - ( x2y1+x3y2+x4y3+x1y4)
U2: quadrilateral is 28 square units whose vertices are taken in the order minus ( -4, - 2 )(- 3,k)(3, - 2)and (2 ,3)
U3: Find the value of k of thequadrilateral is 28 square units whose vertices are taken in the order ( -4, - 2 )(- 3,k)(3, - 2)and (2 ,3)","Using the shoelace formula for the vertices in order 
\((x_1,y_1)=(-4,-2),\ (x_2,y_2)=(-3,k),\ (x_3,y_3)=(3,-2),\ (x_4,y_4)=(2,3)\):

\[
\text{Area}=\frac12\left|\,(x_1y_2+x_2y_3+x_3y_4+x_4y_1)-(x_2y_1+x_3y_2+x_4y_3+x_1y_4)\,\right|
\]

Compute the two sums:

\[
x_1y_2+x_2y_3+x_3y_4+x_4y_1
= (-4)k+(-3)(-2)+(3)(3)+(2)(-2)
= -4k+6+9-4
= -4k+11
\]

\[
x_2y_1+x_3y_2+x_4y_3+x_1y_4
= (-3)(-2)+(3)k+(2)(-2)+(-4)(3)
= 6+3k-4-12
= 3k-10
\]

So
\[
\text{Area}=\frac12\left|(-4k+11)-(3k-10)\right|
=\frac12| -7k+21|
\]

Given area \(=28\):
\[
\frac12| -7k+21|=28
\]
\[
|-7k+21|=56
\]
Factor out 7:
\[
7|3-k|=56
\]
\[
|3-k|=8
\]

So:
\[
3-k=8 \Rightarrow k=-5
\quad \text{or} \quad
3-k=-8 \Rightarrow k=11
\]

**Final: \(\mathbf{k=-5}\) or \(\mathbf{k=11}\).**",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Speech to Text,,,0.9500,13638,261,0.002960,"The bot correctly understood and answered the user's math questions about quadrilaterals and the value of k using the shoelace formula. There are no evident failures or misinterpretations, and the session is purely academic with speech-to-text modality. The user rephrased the question but did not indicate dissatisfaction or correction ignored.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
