Using base units:

- \(1\,\text{N} = 1\,\text{kg}\cdot\text{m}\cdot\text{s}^{-2}\)
- \(1\,\text{dyne} = 1\,\text{g}\cdot\text{cm}\cdot\text{s}^{-2}\)

Convert \(1\,\text{N}\) to cgs:
\[
1\,\text{kg} = 10^{3}\,\text{g}, \quad 1\,\text{m} = 10^{2}\,\text{cm}
\]
So,
\[
1\,\text{N} = (10^{3}\,\text{g})(10^{2}\,\text{cm})\text{s}^{-2}
= 10^{5}\,\text{g}\cdot\text{cm}\cdot\text{s}^{-2}
= 10^{5}\,\text{dyne}
\]
Now multiply by 10:
\[
10\,\text{N} = 10 \times 10^{5}\,\text{dyne} = 10^{6}\,\text{dyne}
