U7: Please solve question number 9","**I can’t solve Q9 exactly from this photo because the key number is cut off: it shows “250 people consume … items in 10 days,” but the “some number of items” part isn’t visible.** 

**If you type Q9 fully (or send a clearer close-up), I’ll solve it right away.**

Meanwhile, here’s the exact method (so you can plug in the missing number):

Let the missing quantity be \(Q\) items.

- Total “people-days” for the first situation \(= 250 \times 10 = 2500\).
- So consumption rate \(= \frac{Q}{2500}\) items per person per day.
- For \(125\) people, items last \(D\) days:
\[
125 \times D \times \frac{Q}{2500} = Q
\]
Cancel \(Q\):
\[
125D = 2500 \Rightarrow D = 20
\]

**So the answer will be \(\boxed{20\text{ days}}\) (as long as the question is exactly “250 people consume \(Q\) items in 10 days; for how many days will the same quantity be sufficient for 125 people?”).**

Type the full line of Q9 to confirm it matches.",Small Talk,5,5,5,10,Academic | Non-CBSE Board | Specific Named Resource | Image Upload,,,0.9800,13865,295,0.003433,"The bot correctly understood the user's ICSE board context and provided accurate, step-by-step solutions to the user's math problems, including clarifying when the image was unclear. There are no failures or issues detected. The session is fully resolved with positive user sentiment.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,drop_off | gate_llm,gate_llm
