## 2) Invitation to a friend for your Birthday Party (Informal)
**Format**
- Address + Date 
- *Dear …,* 
- Invite + date/time/place 
- Special note (dress code/games/food) 
- Ask them to come + confirm 
- *Yours lovingly,* + Name 

**Useful lines**
- “I’m having a small birthday party at my home on ___ at ___.” 
- “Do come—I’ll be very happy if you celebrate with me.”

---

## 3) Congratulations to a friend who topped the school (Informal)
**Key points**
- Congratulate warmly 
- Say you’re proud/happy 
- Praise hard work 
- Wish future success 
- Plan to meet/celebrate 

**Useful lines**
- “Heartiest congratulations on securing the first position in your school.” 
- “Your hard work has really paid off.”

---

## 4) Congrats on selection in NDA Examination (Informal)
**Key points**
- Congratulate 
- Mention discipline/effort 
- Wish success in training and service 
- Encourage to stay focused/humble 

**Useful lines**
- “Congratulations on your selection in the NDA examination.” 
- “I’m sure you’ll make a fine officer and make your family proud.”

---

## 5) Letter to father: what you wish to do after school (Informal)
**Key points**
- Tell your plan (stream/course/career) 
- Reasons (interest/strengths/goals) 
- What steps you’ll take (coaching, reading, routine) 
- Ask for guidance/support respectfully 

**Useful lines**
- “After completing school, I wish to pursue ___ because ___.” 
- “Please guide me and let me know what you think.”

---

## 6) Complaint to the Mayor about stray dogs/monkeys (Formal)
**Format**
- Your address + Date 
- Receiver’s designation/address 
- **Subject:** Complaint about stray dogs/monkeys in ___ 
- Problem + danger/inconvenience 
- Request action (animal control, sterilisation, relocation, awareness) 
- Polite closing + signature 

**Useful lines**
- “I wish to draw your kind attention to the menace of stray ___ in our locality.” 
- “Kindly arrange immediate action to ensure public safety.”

---

## 7) Report theft to S.H.O. (Formal)
**Key points to include**
- Date/time of theft 
- Address and what happened (brief, clear) 
- Items stolen (general list) 
- Any suspects/observations (if any) 
- Request FIR and investigation 

**Useful lines**
- “I request you to register an FIR and take necessary action at the earliest.” 
- “I shall be available for any further information.”

---

