Adding a Slide
A stide refers to a single page in a PowerPoint presentation where content is displayed. It contains placeholders that hold text, titles, bulleted lists, and other objects such as tables, charts, images, movies, and sound clips. While creating a presentation, sometimes you need to insert new slides in it. Whenever you insert a new stide, first select its layout. Let us add a new slide using the following steps:
- Select the slide after which you want to add a new slide.
+ If you want that the new slide should have the same layout as that of the previous one, then click on the New Slide □ button in the Stides group on the Home tab.
- If you want your new slide to be based on any other slide layout, click on the New Slide drop-down arrow. Select the desired slide layout.
\( { }^{-} \)PowerPoint will add a new slide with the selected layout in the Slides pane. It can also be seen in the Slides Navigation Pane on

