U3: No make again in netter way","**Here’s a cleaner, better roadmap for PCM + PE + Yoga.**

### **Daily Roadmap (Mon–Sat)**
**Goal:** 3 PCM sessions + PE/Yoga daily

**Session 1 (2 hours) — Main subject of the day**
- 60 min: concepts/notes + examples 
- 60 min: questions (NCERT + exercise/PYQ)

**Session 2 (1.5 hours) — Second subject**
- 45 min: revise 1 topic/chapter part 
- 45 min: questions

**Session 3 (1 hour) — Third subject (light)**
- 20 min: formula/summary revision 
- 40 min: 10–20 MCQs or 4–6 numericals

**Session 4 (40 min) — PE + Yoga**
- 25 min: PE theory (1 unit/topic + short notes)
- 15 min: Yoga (practice + 5 key points: benefits/precautions/steps)

**Session 5 (20 min) — “Backlog saver” (must do daily)**
- Pick **one old chapter** (any one subject)
- Do **only 15–20 questions OR 1 PYQ set**
- Write mistakes in a small “error copy”

---

### **Subject Rotation (so everything gets covered)**
Use this 3-day cycle and repeat:

- **Day A:** Main Physics → Second Maths → Light Chemistry 
- **Day B:** Main Maths → Second Chemistry → Light Physics 
- **Day C:** Main Chemistry → Second Physics → Light Maths 

Then repeat: A, B, C, A, B, C…

---

### **Sunday Roadmap (Test + Fix day)**
- 2 hours: **1 mock/sample paper** (PCM mixed or single subject)
- 1 hour: check + mark mistakes
- 1 hour: revise only those weak points
- 30 min: PE/Yoga revision

---

### **Weekly Targets (simple and measurable)**
- **Physics:** 2 chapters + 1 test
- **Chemistry:** 2 chapters (split into Physical/Organic/Inorganic as per syllabus) + 1 test
- **Maths:** 2 chapters + 1 test
- **PE:** 2 units per week
- **Yoga:** 4 practice days + 1 theory revision day

---

### **Rules to follow (so backlog doesn’t grow)**
- **No day ends without Session 5 (Backlog saver).**
- Practice > reading: **at least 50% time should be questions.**
- Keep one notebook: **Formula + Errors** (only these two).

---

