Movements of the Earth - their Effects
We have already learnt that the Earth, like all the planets of the solar system, moves around the Sun. Take a globe and spin it from west to east. The Earth also spins in the same way. Now, look at the globe again. You notice that the globe is tilted at a particular angle. Just like the globe, the Earth is also tilted. Now, imagine a line drawn through the centre of the Earth, joining the North and the South Poles. This imaginary line is called the axis of the Earth. The axis is tilted at an angle of \( 661 / 2^{\circ} \) to the plane of the Earth's orbit. The Earth spins from west to east on its axis. Let us find more about its movements.
