REVOLUTION
When rotating on its tilted axis, the Earth also moves around the Sun on a fixed path. This fixed path is called the orbit. The Earth completes one revolution in \( 3651 / 4 \) days. We have only 365 days on our calendar. The \( 1 / 4 \) day of every year is added to make one extra day. This extra day is added every fourth year to the month of February. Hence, February has 29 days every fourth year instead of 28 days. A year with 360 days is known as a leap year. The last leap year was in the year 2020.
