We can use cross-multiplication to compare fractions and find out which is greater.
To find out which of the two fractions is greater, cross-multiply and place the two numbers you get, under the two fractions as shown in the next example.
Example 4: Compare \( \frac{3}{8} \) and \( \frac{5}{12} \).
Solution: Cross multiply the two fractions:

Cross product:
\[
\begin{array}{cc}
\frac{3}{8} & \frac{5}{12} \\
\vdots \\
3 \times 12=36 & 8 \times 5=40
\end{array}
\]

As,
\[
\begin{aligned}
36 & <40 \\
\frac{3}{8} & <\frac{5}{12}
\end{aligned}
\]

