U4: The question is this x³-2x²-x+2 and my answer is (x-2)(x-1)(x+1)","**Yes — that’s correct.**

Start with
\[
x^3-2x^2-x+2
\]
Group terms:
\[
(x^3-2x^2)+(-x+2)
\]
Factor each group:
\[
x^2(x-2)-1(x-2)
\]
Now factor out the common \((x-2)\):
\[
(x-2)(x^2-1)
\]
Use difference of squares:
\[
x^2-1=(x-1)(x+1)
\]
So the factorisation is
\[
\boxed{(x-2)(x-1)(x+1)}
\]",Procedural,1,1,1,2,Academic,,Incorrect Answer | Correction Ignored,0.9500,13241,295,0.003307,"The bot initially gave an incorrect factorisation and failed to correctly resolve the user's query until the last turn. The user corrected the bot's mistake, indicating dissatisfaction and requiring the bot to adjust its response. Despite final resolution, the initial errors and user corrections justify moderate downgrades in reliability and user sentiment.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,correction | gate_llm,gate_llm
e2efec7f-4992-42b1-a657-bdff5073b868,2026-08-18T14:21:11.371Z,31227824,8,"U1: Half the perimeter of a garden whose length is 4 m more than its width is 36 m find the dimensions of the garden it is the question of chapter 3 was name is pair of linear equation in two variable
