Plants can be divided into two main groups terrestrial plants and aquatic plants.

Terrestrial Plants
- Plants that grow on land are called terrestrial plants. There are different types of terrestrial plants that grow in different habitats, such as plains, mountains, deserts, etc.
Plants in Hilly Areas
Plants of hilly areas have special features:
- They are straight, tall and cone-shaped.
- These trees do not have flowers.
- They have woody cones.
- These trees have needle-like leaves.
- Branches of these trees are sloping, so that snow may slide off easily during the cold winter months.
- Mountain trees have a waxy coating on leaves to avoid any damage to them from snow. Some mountain trees are pine, deodar, fir, etc. Besides trees, some other plants are also found in mountain areas, like ferns, mosses, lichens, etc.
