## 6 Celebration-Based Notice Questions (with Titles)

### 1) **Independence Day Celebration**
**Notice Title/Subject:** *Independence Day Celebration – Programme & Participation* 
**Question:** Your school is celebrating Independence Day with flag hoisting, cultural programme, and speeches. Write a notice inviting students to take part. 
**Include:** date/time, venue, rehearsal details, dress code (uniform), last date to give names.

---

### 2) **Teachers’ Day Celebration**
**Notice Title/Subject:** *Teachers’ Day Celebration – Student Performances* 
**Question:** Your class/school is planning a Teachers’ Day programme with skits, songs, and thank-you cards. Write a notice calling for participants. 
**Include:** audition/selection time, event time, venue, teacher-in-charge, rules (decent content, time limit).

---

### 3) **Children’s Day Celebration**
**Notice Title/Subject:** *Children’s Day Celebration – Games & Fun Events* 
**Question:** The school is organizing games, fun contests, and a short cultural programme on Children’s Day. Write a notice for students. 
**Include:** list of events, reporting time, class-wise teams, items to bring (water bottle/cap), instructions.

---

### 4) **Kannada Rajyotsava Celebration**
**Notice Title/Subject:** *Kannada Rajyotsava – Cultural Events & Dress Code* 
**Question:** Your school is celebrating Kannada Rajyotsava with Kannada songs, speech, quiz, and fancy dress/traditional wear. Write a notice. 
**Include:** competitions, eligibility, registration date, dress code, prizes, contact person.

---

### 5) **Annual Day Celebration**
**Notice Title/Subject:** *Annual Day Celebration – Rehearsal Schedule & Participation* 
**Question:** Your school is preparing for Annual Day with dances, drama, and choir. Write a notice inviting students and sharing rehearsal details. 
**Include:** practice dates/timings, selection, venue, discipline instructions, coordinator.

---

### 6) **School Foundation Day**
**Notice Title/Subject:** *School Foundation Day – Celebration & House Activities* 
**Question:** Your school is celebrating its Foundation Day with a special assembly, house-wise activities, and an exhibition. Write a notice. 
**Include:** event schedule, house-wise participation, exhibition details, things to bring (models/charts), deadline.

--- 

