A) \(-1\) B) \(1\) C) \(2\) D) \(-2\)

5) The pair \(2x+3y=7\) and \(4x+6y=14\) has 
A) no solution B) unique solution C) infinitely many solutions D) two solutions

6) For \(a_1x+b_1y=c_1\) and \(a_2x+b_2y=c_2\), unique solution when 
A) \(\dfrac{a_1}{a_2}=\dfrac{b_1}{b_2}=\dfrac{c_1}{c_2}\) 
B) \(\dfrac{a_1}{a_2}\neq\dfrac{b_1}{b_2}\) 
C) \(\dfrac{a_1}{a_2}=\dfrac{b_1}{b_2}\neq\dfrac{c_1}{c_2}\) 
D) \(a_1=a_2\)

7) Discriminant of \(x^2-6x+9=0\) is 
A) \(36\) B) \(0\) C) \(-36\) D) \(18\)

8) Roots of \(x^2-6x+8=0\) are 
A) \(2,4\) B) \(-2,-4\) C) \(3,3\) D) \(1,8\)

9) If sum of zeros of \(2x^2+px+3\) is \(5\), then \(p=\) 
A) \(-10\) B) \(10\) C) \(-5\) D) \(5\)

