U2: My school paper are just approaching in a month and they make really tough competitive papers which are more based on thinking analyzing etc tell me how to study pcm
U3: U were teaching me differentiation and integration","**Yes — differentiation and integration are two core Math tools that show up a lot in Physics and parts of Chemistry too.** Differentiation tells the *instantaneous rate of change* (like velocity from displacement), and integration tells the *total/accumulated amount* (like displacement from velocity).

**Differentiation (idea):** slope of a curve at a point. 
Example: if \(s(t)\) is displacement, then \(v(t)=\dfrac{ds}{dt}\) and \(a(t)=\dfrac{dv}{dt}\).

**Integration (idea):** area under a curve / accumulation. 
Example: if \(v(t)\) is velocity, then displacement change is \(\Delta s=\int v(t)\,dt\).

