-6g-8f=45 \quad\text{and}\quad 22g-4f=35
\]

Eliminate \(f\) without changing the first equation’s sign:

Multiply the second equation by \(2\):
\[
44g-8f=70
\]

Now subtract the first equation from this:
\[
(44g-8f)-(-6g-8f)=70-45
\]
\[
50g=25 \;\Rightarrow\; g=\frac{1}{2}
\]

Substitute \(g=\frac12\) into \(22g-4f=35\):
\[
22\left(\frac12\right)-4f=35
\]
\[
