- Explain one process/diagram from the chapter in **3–4 sentences**.
- Write two safety rules/precautions (if the chapter has them).

## Chapter 2 — Important Questions
- What is the main concept of this chapter? Explain in **2–3 sentences**.
- Define the important terms (any 4–6).
- Draw and label the main diagram (if there is one) and write its use.
- Write **two differences** between two things discussed in the chapter.
- Give **two real-life uses/applications**.

## Chapter 3 — Different Types of Switches (Important)
- What is a **switch**?
- What is the difference between an **open circuit** and a **closed circuit**?
- What happens when a switch is **ON**? What happens when it is **OFF**?
- List different types of switches mentioned in the textbook.
- Explain a **push-button switch** with an example.
- Write two examples each for **conductors** and **insulators**.
- Draw a simple circuit (cell–bulb–switch–wires) and show **open** and **closed** circuit.

