U3: About monohybrid cross here it is not mentioned","**Monohybrid cross** is a genetic cross that studies **one trait at a time** (like only height or only flower color). It’s often taught right after “genes/alleles control traits,” even if your page didn’t use the term.

Here are **more than 20 monohybrid-cross practice questions with answers** (no page needed):

1) **What is a monohybrid cross?** 
A cross between two individuals considering **one pair of contrasting traits**.

2) **What is meant by one pair of contrasting traits?** 
Two different forms of the same trait, like **tall vs short**.

3) **What do the symbols \(T\) and \(t\) usually represent?** 
Two alleles of a gene (often \(T\) = dominant, \(t\) = recessive).

4) **What is a dominant trait?** 
A trait that appears even when only **one dominant allele** is present (e.g., \(Tt\)).

5) **What is a recessive trait?** 
A trait that appears only when **both alleles are recessive** (e.g., \(tt\)).

6) **Define genotype.** 
The allele combination, like \(TT\), \(Tt\), \(tt\).

7) **Define phenotype.** 
The visible/expressed trait, like tall or short.

8) **What is a homozygous genotype? Give examples.** 
Both alleles same: \(TT\) or \(tt\).

9) **What is a heterozygous genotype? Give an example.** 
Two different alleles: \(Tt\).

10) **What is the genotype of a pure tall plant (if tall is dominant)?** 
\(TT\).

11) **What is the genotype of a pure short plant (if short is recessive)?** 
\(tt\).

12) **Cross \(TT \times tt\). What are the F1 genotypes?** 
All offspring are **\(Tt\)**.

13) **In \(TT \times tt\), what is the F1 phenotype (if \(T\) is dominant)?** 
All are **tall**.

14) **What is the F1 generation?** 
The **first filial** generation (offspring of the parental cross).

15) **What is the F2 generation?** 
Offspring produced by **crossing F1 individuals** (often \(Tt \times Tt\)).

16) **Cross \(Tt \times Tt\). List the possible genotypes.** 
\(TT\), \(Tt\), \(Tt\), \(tt\).

17) **In \(Tt \times Tt\), what is the genotypic ratio?** 
**\(1:2:1\)** (1 \(TT\) : 2 \(Tt\) : 1 \(tt\)).

18) **In \(Tt \times Tt\), what is the phenotypic ratio (dominant:recessive)?** 
**\(3:1\)**.

19) **In \(Tt \times Tt\), what fraction are recessive phenotype?** 
\(\frac{1}{4}\) (25%).

20) **In \(Tt \times Tt\), what fraction are heterozygous?** 
\(\frac{2}{4} = \frac{1}{2}\) (50%).

21) **If a tall plant has genotype \(Tt\), what gametes can it produce?** 
Two types: **\(T\)** and **\(t\)**.

22) **If a short plant has genotype \(tt\), what gametes can it produce?** 
Only **\(t\)**.

23) **Test cross: Cross a tall unknown plant \(T?\) with short \(tt\). If all offspring are tall, what is the unknown genotype?** 
Unknown is **\(TT\)** (because \(TT \times tt \rightarrow\) all \(Tt\) tall).

24) **In a test cross \(T? \times tt\), if offspring are 1 tall : 1 short, what is the unknown genotype?** 
Unknown is **\(Tt\)**.

If you tell me the exact trait letters your teacher/textbook uses (like \(A/a\) or \(T/t\)) and the trait (pea height/seed shape/etc.), I’ll rewrite these questions using the same symbols.**",Quiz_request,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Mock / Practice Questions | Image Upload,,,0.9500,13954,276,0.003000,"The bot correctly understood and fulfilled the user's request for extra questions and long answers related to the uploaded biology page. There are no evident failures or mismatches in content or context. The user did not explicitly express satisfaction or dissatisfaction, so user sentiment is neutral.",0,full_rate,Academic,Practice / Quiz,multiple_similar_requests | gate_llm,gate_llm
