*(based on structure and location)*

| Basis | Striated (Skeletal) muscle | Cardiac muscle |
|---|---|---|
| **Shape of fibres** | Long, cylindrical fibres | Shorter cylindrical fibres |
| **Branching** | **Unbranched** | **Branched** and form a network |
| **Striations** | Striations (bands) **present** | Striations **present** |
| **Nucleus** | **Many nuclei** (multinucleate), usually at the edge | **One (sometimes two) nucleus**, central |
| **Special feature** | No intercalated discs | **Intercalated discs present** |
| **Control** | **Voluntary** (under our control) | **Involuntary** (not under our control) |
| **Location in body** | Attached to bones—arms, legs, face, neck, etc. | **Only in the wall of the heart** |

