U3: vrittiya Gati ke liye aavrat kal aur aavritti ki paribhasha AVN Sutra likhiye w 3rd hai Maaf kijiega Mere Samajh Mein Nahin Aaya","**वृत्तीय गति में “आवर्तकाल” और “आवृत्ति” का मतलब और उनके सूत्र:**

**1) आवर्तकाल (Time Period), \(T\)** 
**परिभाषा:** किसी वस्तु को वृत्त में **1 पूरा चक्कर** लगाने में जितना **समय** लगता है, उसे आवर्तकाल कहते हैं। 
**सूत्र:** 
\[
T=\frac{\text{कुल समय}}{\text{चक्करों की संख्या}}
\]
और आवृत्ति के साथ संबंध:
\[
T=\frac{1}{f}
\]
**इकाई:** सेकंड (s)

**2) आवृत्ति (Frequency), \(f\)** 
**परिभाषा:** **1 सेकंड में** वस्तु जितने **पूरे चक्कर** लगाती है, उसे आवृत्ति कहते हैं। 
**सूत्र:** 
\[
f=\frac{\text{चक्करों की संख्या}}{\text{कुल समय}}
\]
और आवर्तकाल के साथ संबंध:
\[
f=\frac{1}{T}
\]
**इकाई:** हर्ट्ज (Hz) \(=\text{s}^{-1}\)

**3) “तीसरा वाला” \( \omega \) (कोणीय वेग) का \(T\) और \(f\) से संबंध** 
वृत्त में **1 पूरा चक्कर = \(2\pi\) rad** (क्योंकि पूरे वृत्त का कोण \(360^\circ = 2\pi\) rad होता है)।

- अगर 1 चक्कर लगाने में समय \(T\) लगे, तो कोणीय वेग:
\[
\omega=\frac{2\pi}{T}
\]

- और क्योंकि \(f=\frac{1}{T}\), इसलिए:
\[
\omega = 2\pi f
\]

यानि एक साथ लिखें तो:
\[
\boxed{\omega = \frac{2\pi}{T} = 2\pi f}
\]

अगर आप बताएं कि आपको \(2\pi\) rad वाला हिस्सा (पूरा चक्कर) समझ नहीं आया या \(f=\frac{1}{T}\) वाला, तो मैं उसी हिस्से को और आसान शब्दों में समझा दूँ।**",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Speech to Text,,,0.9500,13162,264,0.003271,"The bot correctly and clearly answered the user's academic questions about angular velocity and circular motion without any errors or failures. There are no indications of bot failures or user dissatisfaction, though the user rephrased a question for clarity, which is typical in learning contexts. Overall, the session is successful and reliable.",0,full_rate,Academic,Concept Explanation,explicit_frustration | paraphrase_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
c8f9ced6-4c4c-4e8e-9285-88dc8e60fac5,2026-08-18T13:20:06.836Z,1,10,"U1: dout these two effects of electric current. But first let us learn about a source of electric current, the cells. You have read about different types of cells in the previous class especially the dry cell. We will learn some more about cells in the next section.
4.1 CELLS

There are different types of cells that are used for the production of electric current. They do so due to chemical reactions. We will learn about the cells made in the beginning first and then move towards modern cells.

VOLTAIC CELL
A simple Voltaic cell, also known as Galvanic cell, is a device that converts chemical energy into electrical energy. It consists of two metal strips of different metals as electrodes placed in an electrolyte, a liquid solution as shown in the figure. The electrolyte used is normally a dilute acid or salt solution. The reaction between the electrodes and electrolyte results in making one electrode positively charged (cathode) and the other negatively charged (anode). If wires are connected and an electric lamp is placed between them, the electric current starts to flow from cathode ( +ve ) towards anode ( -ve ) making

