U4: Do in array","I can help—but I need one detail: **Do you mean “use an array to store the unique numbers found”**, or **“use an array to check repeated digits”**?

Meanwhile, here’s the **array-storing version** (stores all unique-digit integers in an `int[]` and then prints from the array). 

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class UniqueDigitIntegersArray
{
// Checks if a number has no repeated digits (uses a boolean array)
public static boolean isUnique(int number)
{
boolean[] used = new boolean[10]; // used[d] = true if digit d already appeared

while (number > 0)
{
int digit = number % 10;

if (used[digit]) return false; // repeated digit found

used[digit] = true;
number /= 10;
}
return true;
}

public static void main(String[] args)
{
Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

System.out.print(""INPUT: m = "");
int m = sc.nextInt();
System.out.print(""n = "");
int n = sc.nextInt();

// First pass: count how many unique-digit numbers (so we can create an array of exact size)
int count = 0;
for (int num = m; num 0 && isUnique(num)) count++;
}

// Create array to store the results
int[] uniqueNums = new int[count];

// Second pass: store them in the array
int idx = 0;
for (int num = m; num 0 && isUnique(num))
{
uniqueNums[idx] = num;
idx++;
}
}

// Print using the array
System.out.print(""OUTPUT: THE UNIQUE-DIGIT INTEGERS ARE: "");
for (int i = 0; i < uniqueNums.length; i++)
{
System.out.print(uniqueNums[i] + "" "");
}

System.out.println();
System.out.println(""FREQUENCY OF UNIQUE-DIGIT INTEGERS IS: "" + uniqueNums.length);

sc.close();
}
}
```",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,14668,256,0.003562,"The bot correctly understood and answered the user's programming homework requests with detailed code and explanations, including handling image-based questions. There are no detected failures or misalignments in the conversation. User sentiment is neutral with no explicit positive or negative feedback.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,image_or_prior_context_reask | same_intent_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
