**Until you reply, here are very common Class 12 Chemistry “important question types” (CBSE-style):**
- **Solutions:** Raoult’s law, colligative properties (\(\Delta T_b,\ \Delta T_f,\ \pi\)), van’t Hoff factor, abnormal molar mass.
- **Electrochemistry:** Nernst equation, \(E^\circ_{\text{cell}}\), \(\Delta G^\circ = -nFE^\circ\), cell notation, conductivity vs molar conductivity, Kohlrausch’s law.
- **Chemical Kinetics:** rate law, order, units of \(k\), integrated rate equations (1st order), half-life, Arrhenius equation.
- **Surface Chemistry:** adsorption isotherms (Freundlich), catalysis, colloids (Tyndall effect, coagulation), emulsions.
- **p-Block (15–18):** trends, important compounds (e.g., \(HNO_3\), \(H_2SO_4\), \(NH_3\), halogen oxoacids), interhalogens, anomalous behavior.
- **d- & f-Block:** oxidation states, colour, magnetic moment, \(KMnO_4/K_2Cr_2O_7\) reactions (key ones), lanthanoid contraction.
- **Coordination Compounds:** IUPAC naming, isomerism, CFT (octahedral/tetrahedral), \(\Delta_o\), \(\mu\) (spin-only), hybridization, Werner theory.
- **Haloalkanes & Haloarenes:** SN1 vs SN2, E1/E2, stereochemistry, reactivity order, important conversions.
- **Alcohols, Phenols, Ethers:** acidity of phenols, Lucas test, dehydration/oxidation, Williamson synthesis.
- **Aldehydes, Ketones, Carboxylic Acids:** nucleophilic addition, aldol/Cannizzaro, acidity, HVZ, key tests (Tollens/Fehling/iodoform).
- **Amines:** basicity order, diazotization, coupling, Hoffmann bromamide, key tests.
- **Biomolecules / Polymers / Chemistry in Everyday Life:** structures, differences, uses (high scoring theory).

