cdc993a0-c321-44c3-aab6-865c43ae0e86,2026-08-18T13:02:49.549Z,1,4,"U1: Read Tyler's inspiring story to discover how he transformed the lives of hundreds of underprivileged children in Ghana, rescuing them from the horrors of child trafficking. Then, answer the questions provided.
Tyler Page was just ten years old when he decided to make a big change in the life of another child. Tyler was watching a famous talk show when he got the idea. The show was about children in Ghana, West Africa. Tyler learned that children were being sold by their own parents due to poverty. It is called child trafficking. In Ghana, one in six children aged 4-14 are at risk for being sold into a life of slavery; 2.3 percent of them are forced to work in the fishing industry on Lake Volta. Once the children were bought, they were not treated nicely. They were made to do hard labour. They were not able to have fun. They could only work.
Tyler put himself into the shoes of the children in Ghana. He could not imagine living that kind of life. He knew that he had to help them. Tyler had learnt about Positive Action, a character education program, in school. Positive Action is helping others. It is doing nice things for your community. Tyler decided to use what he learned in school to help someone far away.
Tyler came to know that for just twenty dollars a month he could keep one child from being bought and sold. Tyler set a goal to raise two hundred forty dollars. That would keep one child safe for a year. Tyler held a car wash to raise the money. The car wash was fun and easy. Tyler set a new goal. His new goal was to raise fifty thousand dollars. In just seventeen months, Tyler met that goal as well.

