\[
\begin{array}{l}
(x+a)(x+b)=x^{2}+a x+b x+a b \\
(x+a)(x+b)=x^{2}+(a+b) x+a b
\end{array}
\]
(I) Expansion of \( (x+a)(x+b) \)
\( (x+a) \) and \( (x+b) \) are binomials with one term in common. Let us multiply them.
\[
\begin{aligned}
(x+a)(x+b) & =x(x+b)+a(x+b)=x^{2}+b x+a x+a b \\
& =x^{2}+(a+b) x+a b \\
\therefore \quad(x+a)(x+b) & =x^{2}+(a+b) x+a b
\end{aligned}
\]

