In figure (i), the shape consists of:

- A rectangle of length \(80\text{ m}\)
- Two semicircles whose combined boundary makes one complete circle of diameter \(60\text{ m}\)

The two straight sides contribute:

\[
2 \times 80 = 160\text{ m}
\]

The curved part is the circumference of a circle with diameter \(60\text{ m}\):

\[
\pi d = \pi \times 60 = 60\pi\text{ m}
\]

Therefore,

\[
P=160+60\pi
\]

Using \(\pi \approx 3.14\):

\[
P \approx 160+60(3.14)
\]

\[
P \approx 348.4\text{ m}
\]

\[
\boxed{\textbf{Perimeter of figure (i) } \approx \textbf{348.4 m}}
\]

