Gain \(10\%\) on one \(\Rightarrow\) its cost price \(= \dfrac{S}{1.1}\) 
Loss \(10\%\) on the other \(\Rightarrow\) its cost price \(= \dfrac{S}{0.9}\)

Total CP:
\[
\dfrac{S}{1.1}+\dfrac{S}{0.9}=S\left(\frac{10}{11}+\frac{10}{9}\right)=S\cdot\frac{200}{99}
\]
Total SP \(=2S\)

Overall profit/loss \(\%=\dfrac{2S-\frac{200}{99}S}{\frac{200}{99}S}\times100
=\dfrac{-2}{200}\times100=-1\%\)

