- Started by the British in **1793** (mainly in **Bengal, Bihar, Odisha**).
- It was a system to collect **land revenue (tax)**.
- **Zamindars** were made the **landowners** and tax collectors.
- The land revenue to be paid to the Company was **fixed** for a long time.
- Zamindars had to pay the fixed amount **on time every year**.
- If they did not pay, their land could be **taken away and auctioned**.
- Zamindars collected rent from **peasants (farmers)**.
- Many peasants suffered because rent was often **high** and they had **little protection**.",NA,1,1,1,2,Academic | Not Math/Science | Image Upload | Speech to Text,,Correction Ignored | Completion Refusal,0.9500,14811,417,0.003792,"The bot correctly identified the academic subject and modality but repeatedly refused to provide direct pointwise answers, causing user frustration and repeated re-asks. This refusal and failure to fulfill the user's request led to a low goal resolution and user sentiment score. There were no technical failures or context handling issues.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,same_intent_reask | paraphrase_reask | multiple_similar_requests | explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
