**But I *can* help you make it on paper—here’s what your diagram should look like (what to draw):**

- Draw **\(CD=6\text{ cm}\)** as a straight horizontal line (C on the left, D on the right).
- At **C**, draw a ray going up-left so that **\(\angle BCD = 155^\circ\)** (this makes \(BC\) almost in the opposite direction from \(CD\)).
- Mark **B** on that ray such that **\(BD=5\text{ cm}\)** (use compass from D, radius 5 cm, to cut the ray).
- At **B**, draw **\(BA\)** so that **\(\angle ABD = 125^\circ\)** (with \(BD\) as one arm).
- On that ray, mark **\(A\)** so that **\(AB=6\text{ cm}\)**.
- Join **A to D** and **A to C** to finish the quadrilateral.

