- **Break (5 min)**
- **Block B (25 min):** Close the book and **recall-write**: definitions, steps of any process, and 2–3 differences (if any). Then check and fix.
- **Break (5 min)**
- **Block C (15 min):** Do **questions** (end-of-chapter or past paper). Mark wrong ones in a “mistake list.”

**2) How to study Biology so your focus stays high**
- Don’t “re-read” for long. Biology feels familiar but doesn’t stick unless you **test yourself**.
