of the magnet that points towards north direction","**Here are the correct answers (with quick help so it’s clear):**

### **A. Multiple Choice Questions**

1) **Which is an example of a magnetic substance?** 
Nickel, cobalt (and iron) are magnetic, so the best option is **d. All of these**

2) **Which of the following is a use of magnets?** 
Magnets are used to lift/handle iron objects and separate iron from waste, so the best match is **a. Crane in motors** (it looks like “crane in motions” in your text).

3) **Which materials are attracted to a magnet?** 
Only magnetic materials get attracted, so **a. Magnetic materials**

4) **What are the two poles of a magnet?** 
**a. North and South**

5) **When a bar magnet is brought near iron dust, most dust sticks…** 
At the poles (the ends), so **c. Near two ends**

---

### **B. One-Word Answers**

1) Device used to find direction: **Compass** 
2) Loss of magnetism over time: **Demagnetisation** 
3) Materials that get attracted towards the magnet: **Magnetic materials** 
4) Pole of the magnet that points towards north direction: **North pole**

