9d14f21c-4278-4cbe-8554-e9fb3b1e521b,2026-08-18T12:09:10.180Z,1,3,"U1: How to solve this question in easy

A physics multiple-choice problem asks how much ice melts when a 2 kg copper block, heated to 500°C, is placed on a large block of ice at 0°C. Use the heat released by cooling copper and the latent heat of fusion of ice.
U2: How to solve this question in easy way
U3: How to solve this question in easy way

A physics multiple-choice problem asks how much ice at 0°C melts when 80 g of water at 30°C is poured onto it. It involves heat transfer and the latent heat of fusion.","When the \(80\ \text{g}\) of water cools from \(30^\circ\text{C}\) to \(0^\circ\text{C}\), it releases heat:

\[
Q = mc\Delta T
\]

\[
Q = 80 \times 1 \times 30 = 2400\ \text{cal}
\]

This heat melts some ice. Using the latent heat of fusion of ice,

\[
Q = mL
\]

\[
2400 = m \times 80
\]

\[
m = \frac{2400}{80} = 30\ \text{g}
\]

Therefore, the mass of ice that melts is **\(30\ \text{g}\)** — **Option A**.",Procedural,5,5,5,10,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,12926,251,0.003216,"The bot correctly answered all user questions with detailed, accurate physics solutions based on the provided images. There are no indications of bot failures, context issues, or user dissatisfaction. The session is a straightforward academic help session with image uploads.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,multiple_similar_requests | gate_llm,gate_llm
