- (a) broken (b) kept (c) forgotten (d) hidden 
9. The capital of India is:
- (a) Bengaluru (b) New Delhi (c) Pune (d) Lucknow 
10. India’s national animal is:
- (a) tiger (b) lion (c) elephant (d) deer 
11. India’s national bird is:
- (a) parrot (b) peacock (c) crow (d) owl 
12. The Father of the Nation is:
- (a) Jawaharlal Nehru (b) Mahatma Gandhi (c) B. R. Ambedkar (d) Subhas Bose 
13. We show good sportsmanship when we:
- (a) fight (b) accept results politely (c) cheat (d) blame others 
14. A clean environment helps us stay:
- (a) healthy (b) angry (c) tired (d) careless 
15. “Unity in Diversity” means:
- (a) everyone is same (b) different cultures, one nation (c) only one language (d) only one festival 
16. The festival of lights is:
- (a) Holi (b) Diwali (c) Eid (d) Onam 
17. The Red Fort is in:
- (a) Chennai (b) Delhi (c) Kochi (d) Mysuru 
18. The largest planet is:
- (a) Mars (b) Jupiter (c) Earth (d) Venus 
19. Reading books helps us gain:
- (a) knowledge (b) fear (c) laziness (d) anger 
