U3: Not numericals but they with diagram","**I can’t provide an answer key with finished diagrams.** But I *can* give you **diagram-based practice questions**, and then you can send a photo of your ray diagrams and I’ll check/correct them.

**Ray-diagram practice questions (no numericals):**

1) **Convex lens:** Object placed **beyond \(2F_1\)**. 
Draw the ray diagram using any two principal rays and label \(F_1, 2F_1, O, F_2, 2F_2\). State the image position and nature.

2) **Convex lens:** Object placed **at \(2F_1\)**. 
Draw and state image position, size, and nature.

3) **Convex lens:** Object placed **between \(F_1\) and \(2F_1\)**. 
Draw and state image position, size, and nature.

4) **Convex lens:** Object placed **at \(F_1\)**. 
Draw and state what happens to the image (where it forms).

5) **Convex lens:** Object placed **between \(O\) and \(F_1\)**. 
Draw and state image position and nature.

6) **Concave lens:** Object placed anywhere on the left of the lens. 
Draw and state image position and nature.

7) In a **convex lens diagram**, show these two rays from the top of the object: 
(a) a ray **parallel** to the principal axis, 
(b) a ray passing through the **optical center \(O\)**. 
Complete the diagram and locate the image.

8) In a **convex lens diagram**, use the ray: 
(a) passing through \(F_1\) before refraction becomes **parallel** after refraction, 
(b) one ray through \(O\). 
Locate the image for the case “object between \(F_1\) and \(2F_1\)”.

9) **Compare by diagrams:** Draw one ray diagram each to show why a **convex lens can form a real image on a screen** but a **concave lens cannot** (for a real object).

10) **Defect/correction diagram (basic):** Draw the ray diagram to show how a **concave lens corrects myopia** (short-sightedness). (Just the idea: diverging lens makes rays appear to come from farther.)

Pick **any one number (1–10)**, draw it, and upload a photo—then I’ll tell you exactly what to fix (labels, rays, and where the image should be).",Unit Conversion,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Mock / Practice Questions | Specific Named Resource,,,0.9500,13078,268,0.003232,"The bot correctly understood and responded to the user's academic requests with relevant practice questions and explanations. There were no failures or misalignments in content or context. The user did not express dissatisfaction or re-ask due to failure, so user sentiment is neutral.",0,full_rate,Academic,Practice / Quiz,correction | gate_llm,gate_llm
