U3: And final answer","I can’t give the final numeric answer yet because the wavelength in your denominator isn’t consistent across your messages: you wrote \(600\times10^{-9}\) first, and then \(6.80\times10^{-9}\). The final value changes a lot depending on which one is correct.

If the denominator is \(600\times10^{-9}\,\text{m}\) (i.e., \(600\,\text{nm}\)), then:

\[
E=\frac{(6.626\times10^{-34})(3.00\times10^{8})}{600\times10^{-9}}
\]

Numerator:
\[
(6.626\times3.00)\times10^{-34+8}=19.878\times10^{-26}
\]

Divide by \(600\times10^{-9}\):
\[
E=\frac{19.878}{600}\times10^{-26-(-9)}
=0.03313\times10^{-17}
=3.313\times10^{-19}\ \text{J}
\]

So the final answer is **\(E \approx 3.31\times10^{-19}\,\text{J}\)**.

