## Advanced Practice: Simple Tenses

### 1) Error correction (find and fix the mistake)
1. She **go** to coaching every evening. 
2. We **will goes** to the library tomorrow. 
3. They **didn’t visited** the museum last week. 
4. My brother **don’t** like spicy food. 
5. I **see** him yesterday at the market. 
6. The class **start** at 9:00 a.m. every day.

---

### 2) Choose the best tense (watch for time words)
7. Every year, our school ______ (conduct / conducted / will conduct) a sports day in December. 
8. I ______ (meet / met / will meet) my cousin last Sunday. 
9. Look at those clouds! I think it ______ (rain / rained / will rain). 
10. My parents usually ______ (travel / traveled / will travel) by train. 
11. The teacher ______ (check / checked / will check) our notebooks tomorrow.

---

### 3) Rewrite (change the tense as instructed)
12. *(Change to simple past)* “I play badminton.” → __________________________ 
13. *(Change to simple future)* “She cooks dinner.” → __________________________ 
14. *(Change to simple present)* “They visited Chennai.” → __________________________ 
15. *(Change to simple past)* “We will watch the match.” → __________________________ 

---

### 4) Sentence building (use the words + correct simple tense)
16. (Riya / not / drink / coffee / every day) 
17. (I / finish / the project / yesterday evening) 
18. (They / buy / a new phone / next week) 
19. (The sun / rise / in the east) 
20. (We / not / go / to school / last Monday)

---

### 5) Mini editing task (keep only simple tenses)
**Edit the paragraph so it uses ONLY simple present, simple past, or simple future.** 
