## Factors that influence the climate of India
- **Latitude** (how far a place is from the Equator)
- **Altitude** (higher places are cooler)
- **Distance from the sea** (coastal areas have mild climate; inland areas have extreme climate)
- **Relief features/mountains** (Himalayas block cold winds; Western Ghats affect rainfall)
- **Monsoon winds & pressure systems** (seasonal wind changes bring rain)
- **Jet streams & western disturbances** (affect winter weather, especially in north India)
- **Ocean influence** (surrounding seas and currents affect coastal climate)",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Not Math/Science | Specific Named Resource | Speech to Text,,,0.9500,14564,308,0.003675,The bot consistently answered the user's geography questions accurately and clearly without any failures or misunderstandings. The user rephrased questions multiple times likely due to speech-to-text input but the bot handled all queries well. There are no detected bot failures or issues in this session.,0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,same_intent_reask | drop_off | gate_llm,gate_llm
