For example, **groundwater** is renewable when rain replenishes it. But excessive pumping, pollution, and wastage can make clean groundwater unavailable for a very long time.

Actions to prevent this include:

- using resources carefully and avoiding wastage;
- protecting forests, soil, rivers, and groundwater;
- preventing pollution;
- planting trees and restoring damaged ecosystems;
- using rainwater harvesting and recycling water;
- following sustainable fishing, farming, and grazing practices.

