A handwritten arithmetic problem labeled “(c)” showing the numbers 105, 195, and 65 with an attempted factorization or division procedure using a factor table.","You’ve started a common-divisor/ladder method, which is a sensible approach. I can read the numbers as approximately \(105, 195, 65\). The step where you use \(2\) needs fixing: all three numbers are odd, so dividing them by \(2\) cannot give whole-number results. In this method, each divisor must divide every number in that row exactly. Go back to the first divisor, choose a common factor of all three numbers, and then continue checking each row before writing the next one. Also recheck the last line, since one incorrect divisor makes the final result unreliable.",Procedural,4,5,3,8,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,13025,260,0.003230,"The bot correctly answered the initial LCM question and provided helpful guidance on the image-based factorization method without any factual or procedural errors. There were no bot failures or user complaints, and the session maintained relevant academic focus with image uploads. The user sentiment is neutral with no explicit frustration or praise.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm | last_bot_refusal_stall,gate_llm
