c3c58de8-b25c-4025-9e48-7bf549a83302,2026-08-18T07:21:17.579Z,1,7,"U1: How can I study maths because I have my half yearly exam in September and I haven't seen the book yrrrr😭
U2: Isc class 11
U3: Isc
U4: Provide me all formulas then of ml agrawal
U5: 1
U6: Generate video for explanation
U7: Explain me like my teacher in hindi english bothh","**Trigonometry (Formula Revision) — Hinglish teacher-style**

Trigonometry ka main idea ye hai: **angle \(\theta\)** ke saath triangle ke **side ratios** relate hote hain. Matlab angle badlega to sides ka ratio predictable way me badlega.

**1) Basic ratios (SOH-CAH-TOA)**
Right triangle me:
- \(\sin\theta = \dfrac{\text{Perpendicular}}{\text{Hypotenuse}}\) (SOH)
- \(\cos\theta = \dfrac{\text{Base}}{\text{Hypotenuse}}\) (CAH)
- \(\tan\theta = \dfrac{\text{Perpendicular}}{\text{Base}}\) (TOA)

Hindi me: 
- **sin** = “lamb / tircha” (perpendicular/hypotenuse) 
- **cos** = “paas wali side / tircha” (base/hypotenuse) 
- **tan** = “lamb / paas” (perpendicular/base)

**2) Reciprocal (ulta) ratios**
Agar fraction ko ulta kar do:
- \(\cosec\theta = \dfrac{1}{\sin\theta}\)
- \(\sec\theta = \dfrac{1}{\cos\theta}\)
- \(\cot\theta = \dfrac{1}{\tan\theta}\)

**3) Sabse important identity**
\[
\sin^2\theta + \cos^2\theta = 1
\]
Teacher-style meaning: “Right triangle ke ratios aise set hain ki sin aur cos ka square add karo to hamesha 1 aata hai.”

Isse do aur banti hain:
\[
1+\tan^2\theta=\sec^2\theta,\qquad 1+\cot^2\theta=\cosec^2\theta
\]

**4) Complementary angles (90° wala rule)**
“90° − \(\theta\)” pe **sin aur cos swap** ho jaate hain:
- \(\sin(90^\circ-\theta)=\cos\theta\)
- \(\cos(90^\circ-\theta)=\sin\theta\)
- \(\tan(90^\circ-\theta)=\cot\theta\)

Simple yaad: **co-function**: sin ↔ cos, tan ↔ cot, sec ↔ cosec.

**5) Plus-minus formulas (compound angles)**
Ye Class 11 ka big step hai:
\[
\sin(A+B)=\sin A\cos B+\cos A\sin B
\]
\[
\cos(A+B)=\cos A\cos B-\sin A\sin B
\]
\[
\tan(A+B)=\frac{\tan A+\tan B}{1-\tan A\tan B}
\]
Minus case me signs change similarly:
- \(\sin(A-B)=\sin A\cos B-\cos A\sin B\)
- \(\cos(A-B)=\cos A\cos B+\sin A\sin B\)
- \(\tan(A-B)=\dfrac{\tan A-\tan B}{1+\tan A\tan B}\)

**6) Double angle (A ko 2A bana do)**
\[
\sin 2A=2\sin A\cos A
\]
\[
\cos 2A=\cos^2A-\sin^2A=2\cos^2A-1=1-2\sin^2A
\]
\[
\tan 2A=\frac{2\tan A}{1-\tan^2A}
\]

**English one-line wrap-up:** 
Trigonometry is mostly about **remembering core identities** and using them to **convert or simplify** expressions.

Aapko video-like explanation kis part pe chahiye—**compound angles** (A±B) ya **double angle** (2A)? I’ll explain that part with one short example.",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Non-CBSE Board | Specific Named Resource,,,1.0000,16023,300,0.003857,"The conversation is a clear academic session focused on ISC Class 11 mathematics exam preparation and formula explanations. The user explicitly named a non-CBSE board, so the Non-CBSE Board category applies. There are no bot failures or issues detected; the bot responded appropriately and did not push any unwanted templates or ignore context.",0,full_rate,Academic,Summary / Notes,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
