U7: \begin{aligned}@^{card}\\or\end{aligned}","**It looks like you pasted a broken/unfinished LaTeX command.** In LaTeX:

- `\begin{aligned} ... \end{aligned}` is used to line up multiple equations.
- `@{...}` is only used **inside an alignment environment** like `aligned/align` to control the spacing between columns (it replaces the usual space between `&` alignment points).
- `^{...}` is a **superscript**, and `\card` is not a standard LaTeX command unless you defined it yourself.

Here are a couple of correct patterns, depending on what you meant:

1) If you wanted text as a superscript:
\[
x^{\text{card}}
\]

2) If you wanted to align two lines with an “or” between them:
\[
\begin{aligned}
x &= 3 \\
\text{or } x &= 5
\end{aligned}
\]

3) If you were trying to customize spacing with `@{...}` (must include `&` alignment points):
\[
\begin{aligned}
a & = b @{\quad} \text{or} @{\quad} c & = d
\end{aligned}
\]
(If this doesn’t compile, tell me what exact layout you want—`@{...}` is a bit picky.)

**What are you trying to typeset—an “or” between two equations, or a superscript like “card”?** If you paste the full line you want to display, I can fix the LaTeX exactly.",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic,,,0.9500,13681,232,0.003349,"The bot correctly identified the user's vague math inputs and provided clarifications and explanations in both English and Bengali without any factual or procedural errors. There were no bot failures or misunderstandings, and the user did not express frustration or dissatisfaction. The session is purely academic with no modality or flow tags triggered.",0,full_rate,Academic,Concept Explanation,paraphrase_reask | multiple_similar_requests | gate_llm,gate_llm
