U6: Hm","**Mathematical Logic (Logic + basic Set ideas) से ही शुरू करते हैं।** 

**(A) Statements (वाक्य)**
- **Statement** = ऐसा वाक्य जो साफ़-साफ़ **True या False** हो।
- Examples: 
- “\(2\) is even” → True (statement) 
- “Close the door” → command, True/False नहीं → **statement नहीं** 
- “\(x>3\)” → \(x\) पता नहीं → True/False fixed नहीं → **statement नहीं** (open sentence)

**(B) Negation (NOT)**
- अगर statement \(p\) है, तो “not \(p\)” को \(\lnot p\) लिखते हैं।
- Example: 
\(p\): “5 is prime” (True) 
\(\lnot p\): “5 is not prime” (False)

**(C) AND / OR**
- \(p \land q\) (AND): दोनों True हों तभी True 
- \(p \lor q\) (OR): कम-से-कम एक True हो तो True 
(यहाँ OR का मतलब inclusive OR होता है)

Example: 
\(p\): “\(6\) is even” (T) 
\(q\): “\(6\) is divisible by \(3\)” (T) 
\(p \land q\) = T, \(p \lor q\) = T

**(D) Implication (If…then)**
- “If \(p\), then \(q\)” को \(p \to q\) लिखते हैं। 
- ये **सिर्फ एक case में False** होता है: जब \(p\) True हो और \(q\) False हो। 
बाकी सब में True माना जाता है।

Example: 
\(p\): “Number is multiple of 4” 
\(q\): “Number is even” 
\(p \to q\) True है (क्योंकि multiple of 4 हमेशा even होता है)

---

अब एक छोटा check: इनमें से कौन-कौन **statement** हैं? 
1) “\(7\) is an odd number.” 
2) “Do your homework.” 
3) “\(x+2=5\)” 

बस 1,2,3 के सामने लिख दो: **statement / not a statement**.",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Non-CBSE Board | Specific Named Resource,,,0.9800,14547,295,0.003560,"The conversation is an academic session focused on Maharashtra HSC Maths study guidance and concept explanations. The user explicitly named a non-CBSE board, so the Non-CBSE Board tag applies. There are no bot failures or issues detected; the bot provides relevant, accurate, and contextually appropriate responses throughout.",0,full_rate,Academic,Study Plan / Syllabus,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
