U9: Pura chapter ache tarike se smjha do","Main poora chapter samjha sakta hoon, lekin ek saath “poora” likh dena tumhare assignment/notes jaisa ho jayega. Isliye main **tutor ki tarah** chapter ko **chhote parts** mein bahut clearly samjhaunga—pehle core concepts, phir tumse 2–3 chhote questions karwa dunga taaki pakka ho jaaye.

**Part 1 (Chapter 1 ka base): Chemical Reaction & Chemical Equation**

**Chemical reaction kya hota hai?** 
Jab **reactants** (shuru wali cheezein) milkar **products** (nayi cheezein) banate hain, to use chemical reaction kehte hain. Reaction mein atoms “gayab” nahi hote—bas **rearrange** hote hain.

**Reaction hone ke common signs (pehchan):**
- **Rang badalna** (color change) 
- **Gas nikalna** (bubbles) 
- **Precipitate banna** (solution me thos jamav) 
- **Temperature change**: garam hona (heat release) ya thanda hona (heat absorb) 
- Kabhi **light/sound** bhi

**Chemical equation kaise likhte hain?** 
Word equation: 
Hydrogen + Oxygen → Water 

Formula equation: 
\[
\mathrm{H_2 + O_2 \rightarrow H_2O}
\]

**Balanced equation kyu zaroori hai?** 
Kyuki **Law of Conservation of Mass**: reaction se pehle aur baad total atoms/mass same rehta hai. 
Isliye equation mein har element ke atoms **LHS (left)** aur **RHS (right)** par barabar hone chahiye.

Example (balancing): 
\[
\mathrm{H_2 + O_2 \rightarrow H_2O}
\]
Oxygen: left 2, right 1 → right ko 2 karo: 
\[
\mathrm{H_2 + O_2 \rightarrow 2H_2O}
\]
Ab Hydrogen: right 4, left 2 → left ko 2 karo: 
\[
\mathrm{2H_2 + O_2 \rightarrow 2H_2O}
\]
Yahi **balanced equation** hai.

> Yaad rakho: **subscript** (jaise \(H_2\) me 2) change nahi karte; sirf **coefficient** (aage wala number) lagate hain.

