U17: Is there any other trick for these","**Yes—two easy “tricks” are (1) convert everything to decimals, or (2) combine the hundredths first.**

**1) Decimal method (often fastest)**
Turn the mixed parts into decimals:
\[
32\frac{6}{100}\frac{5}{100}=32+\frac{6}{100}+\frac{5}{100}=32+0.06+0.05=32.11
\]
\[
17\frac{8}{100}\frac{9}{100}=17+0.08+0.09=17.17
\]
Now subtract:
\[
32.11-17.17=14.94
\]

**2) “Add the hundredths first” method**
Combine the two hundredths on each number:
\[
\frac{6}{100}+\frac{5}{100}=\frac{11}{100},\quad \frac{8}{100}+\frac{9}{100}=\frac{17}{100}
\]
So it becomes:
\[
32\frac{11}{100}-17\frac{17}{100}
\]
Then subtract (borrow 1 whole \(=\frac{100}{100}\) if needed) to get \(14\frac{94}{100}\).

